  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological activity against KYSE-140 through multiple, interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets KYSE-140. This indicates a direct, mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and the disease entity KYSE-140, mediated by a common intermediate. Similarly, Mollicellin N is also shown to target A704, which is also involved in the same pathway, reinforcing the consistency of the relationship. The presence of multiple targets in the same pathway suggests that the mechanism of action may involve the inhibition of a shared biological process, potentially affecting cellular signaling or metabolic pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mollicellin N to exert its effects through a common molecular mechanism, which could be relevant in the development of targeted therapies for KYSE-140. The evidence is supported by a consistent pattern of target interactions, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
